        "original_id": "ad96c495-0915-5290-af02-0d1eaa2d1570",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Der Freischütz, Il trovatore, Magic Hunter\n- People: Carl Maria von Weber, Friedrich Kind, Giuseppe Verdi, Salvadore Cammarano, Antonio García Gutiérrez, Ildikó Enyedi, Giovanni Guicciardi\n- Roles: Count di Luna\n- Topics: opera, film adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- Der Freischütz, Op. 77, J. 277, is a German opera with spoken dialogue in three acts by Carl Maria von Weber and a libretto by Friedrich Kind.\n- Antonio García Gutiérrez wrote the 1836 play El trovador, which later served as the basis for Il trovatore.\n- Il trovatore is an opera in four acts by Giuseppe Verdi with an Italian libretto largely written by Salvadore Cammarano.\n- Giovanni Guicciardi created the role of Count di Luna in Verdi's Il trovatore.\n- Magic Hunter is a 1994 Hungarian-Swiss-French fantasy film written and directed by Ildikó Enyedi.\n- Magic Hunter was loosely inspired by the opera Der Freischütz.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "179e7f2d-cd44-584c-82cb-a5ccd70ae8d5",
        "text": "Page: Der Freischütz. Sentence: Der Freischütz , Op. 77, J. 277, (usually translated as \"The Marksman\" or \"The Freeshooter\") is a German opera with spoken dialogue in three acts by Carl Maria von Weber with a libretto by Friedrich Kind.\nPage: Il trovatore. Sentence: Il trovatore (] ; Italian for \"The Troubadour\") is an opera in four acts by Giuseppe Verdi to an Italian libretto largely written by Salvadore Cammarano, based on the play \"El trovador\" (1836) by Antonio García Gutiérrez.\nPage: Magic Hunter. Sentence: Magic Hunter (Hungarian: \"Bűvös vadász\" , French: \"Freischütz\" ) is a 1994 Hungarian-Swiss-French fantasy film written and directed by Ildikó Enyedi and loosely inspired to the opera Der Freischütz.\nPage: Giovanni Guicciardi. Sentence: He is most remembered today for having created the role of Count di Luna in Verdi's \"Il trovatore\", although he created several other leading roles in operas by lesser known Italian composers.",
